{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Upāli","html":"<article id='thag3.11'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 3.11 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 3.11 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tikanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Threes </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Paṭhamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter One </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Upālittheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Upāli </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Saddhāya abhinikkhamma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One newly gone forth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>navapabbajito navo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who has left their home out of faith, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mitte bhajeyya kalyāṇe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>should mix with spiritual friends, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>suddhājīve atandite. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who are tireless and pure of livelihood. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saddhāya abhinikkhamma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One newly gone forth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>navapabbajito navo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who has left their home out of faith, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅghasmiṁ viharaṁ bhikkhu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a mendicant staying in the Saṅgha, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sikkhetha vinayaṁ budho. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>being wise, would train in monastic discipline. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saddhāya abhinikkhamma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One newly gone forth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>navapabbajito navo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who has left their home out of faith, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kappākappesu kusalo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>skilled in what is appropriate and what is not, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>careyya apurakkhato”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>would wander undistracted. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Upālitthero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
